"value":0,"status":"ok","source_url":"https://api.steampowered.com/ISteamUserStats/GetNumberOfCurrentPlayers/v1/?appid=5243210","error_code":null}],"events":[{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1847286114039144","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"One developer against the Swarm: how Kepler Protocol gets developed and tested","summary":"{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46097557/08aee707d9d3bc223de02be8a9ad95ac7f2d47fb.png Kepler Protocol is made without a team: one developer, no test lab, no QA department. Even so, the game is played, checked and measured day and night. Three engines that grew alongside the game make that possible. Three engines instead of a team Setzwerk is the world. The colony, the Swarm and the native Kepler life follow fixed rules and keep running without a player. That is why bots can play complete games under the same","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-24T08:44:09Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114039144","verified_at":"2026-10-24T11:36:37Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1847286114029151","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"update","title":"Demo update 0.9.44 — a clear goal, and the swarm comes","summary":"Thank you for your feedback from Next Fest — many of you told us the goal was unclear and the swarm never showed up. Version 0.9.44 answers both. Everything from 0.9.43 and earlier follows below. Goal — at landing the staff sets you a clear goal: \"Establish a bridgehead — survey the Flux core\". The hint bar shows it with its three steps and suggests a next step — how you get there is up to you. The swarm comes — the threat now builds up step by step: first tracks near the colony, then scouts, fi","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-21T15:03:35Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1847286114029151","verified_at":"2026-10-21T17:59:23Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1846651706687079","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"update","title":"Demo update 0.9.42 — for the start of Next Fest","summary":"For the start of Next Fest: version 0.9.42. Everything from 0.9.41 and 0.9.40 follows below. Event cards — report pictures now lie on the paper as hand-coloured photographs – with a photo border and a caption; Main effort — \"Secure Landing Zone\" now asks for 7 instead of 9 biomes discovered. Drilling — at a suspected vein the drilling rig only stands while a formation next to it is drilling. Once it moves on, the borehole and the core box remain. From 0.9.41 Battle — you can now also move the ca","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-18T14:23:25Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846651706687079","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1846018067925327","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"Fifteen Weeks on Kepler-186e","summary":"The demo is here. It ends exactly where the game begins — and that is on purpose.Starting today you can play Kepler Protocol. Not all of it — the first fifteen weeks. The demo is free and waiting on the store page, in time for Steam Next Fest from October 19 to 26.The version number sits in the bottom left of the main menu. Right now it reads 0.9.28, the twenty-ninth build since the first demo build on September 11. This issue covers what those fifteen weeks contain, what changed in the last few","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-10-07T08:07:43Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1846018067925327","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1841579228671512","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"Six out of Twenty-Nine","summary":"For two devblogs running we promised the same thing: the drill is next. Here it is. It no longer wins on its own — but it no longer loses unnoticed either.{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46097557/f7c74211caa7f0cee77e895e2298510af290e9ef.pngThe Empire can win on Kepler in three ways. It can hold out for seventy turns until the fortress stands. It can storm the Alpha Nest — get in, strike down the queen, hold for three turns. Or it can fire up the planetary core drill and settle the question for good.Twice now","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-22T14:27:11Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1841579228671512","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1839676055893103","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"We're joining Next Fest — and taking more time for the launch","summary":"In October you can play Kepler Protocol. In November you can buy it.Two pieces of news that belong together.The first: a demo in OctoberKepler Protocol will be part of Steam Next Fest, 19–26 October. For one week there'll be a playable demo — the landing on Kepler-186e, the first scouting moves, building a colony under a red sun.For us that's the more important half of this announcement. So far you've been reading about Kepler Protocol. In October you'll have your hand on the lever.The second: E","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-08-02T18:02:03Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1839676055893103","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1839676055888031","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"The Army Nobody Saw Die","summary":"We spent a night playing 540 games against ourselves. What we were looking for, we didn't find. What we found was worse.{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/46097557/f184966bf6feeb1eabad8ab5a5e9ffa17b1ef148.pngKepler Protocol isn't only tested by hand. We have a second system that plays the game when nobody is watching: two AI sides, the full rulebook, real maps — and a log that records every turn. Every resource level, every march order, every crisis.On the night of 31 July, that system ran for eleven hours. 27 ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-07-31T12:34:19Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1839676055888031","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1837955055361017","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"What Falls Does Not Fully Return","summary":"Across thousands of games no one died in our battles. The casualty counter lied. Not this time.A battle in Kepler Protocol is fought, won or lost, formations break — and afterwards, in the report, a number: the fallen. Across thousands of test games that number read zero. On both sides. Not one soldier who failed to come home. The formations dissolved, but the people in them went nowhere — they had never existed, on paper.It was a silent bug, slipped in during a rebuild of the combat system. The","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-07-12T12:03:15Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1837955055361017","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1835871199309124","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"The Swarm Matures","summary":"We have dissected the Swarm once before: how it decides — no commander, only pheromone gradients. Today is about how it grows up. In one test game the Swarm tipped into a war mood after barely two months — the pheromone field glowing, swarms boiling outward, the brood chambers pulsing. An Imperial patrol pushed in, expecting armoured beetles. It found leaping predators. Small, fast, biting things — and nothing else. The heavy legions the Swarm is feared for were not there. They arrived months la","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-06-20T11:06:08Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1835871199309124","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1834602721195456","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"The Core Drill","summary":"For seventeen thousand games the Kaiserreich's greatest structure never once fired. The drill was not to blame.The planetary core drill is outright victory. A monument of Krupp steel and flux that grinds through the planet's crust into the Swarm's brood chamber — activate it, and Kepler-186e is yours. That is the design. Yet across our test runs — seventeen thousand simulated games — it never once sprang to life. Zero activations in the logs.We looked for the fault where you would expect it: in ","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-06-07T08:11:46Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1834602721195456","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1833334318576908","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"Ordo Arachnis — Where Command Ends","summary":"When the enemy has no mind yet still decides. In a test round of Kepler Protocol, an Imperial reconnaissance patrol observed a swarm-pack two fields away. The pack was heading north — direction clear, pace steady. Then, mid-movement, it turned west. No visible cause. No order from anywhere.We searched the log for a directive. There was none. There was a gradient instead: a few fields further west the pheromone concentration had shifted the previous turn — a spore plain had burnt out. The pack di","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-05-25T10:52:03Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1833334318576908","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"},{"id":"steam-steam-4579930-1832065502819153","game_id":"steam-4579930","kind":"announcement","title":"Mission Command — When the AI Decides Its Own Moves","summary":"In an early playtest of Kepler Protocol, the Kaiserreich's main army stood in front of Hive Beta. Fully manned, in combat, pinned. Back at the home base: a barracks, a reserve pool of soldiers, the material for a second corps. The AI saw all of it. And did nothing. That was a poor default we'd built ourselves: one brigade per turn when the army had room. If not — standstill. No matter how clear the situation was. We solved it with an old Prussian principle: Auftragstaktik (mission command). Molt","occurred_at":null,"published_at":"2026-05-10T11:34:00Z","time_precision":"minute","source_url":"https://steamstore-a.akamaihd.net/news/externalpost/steam_community_announcements/1832065502819153","verified_at":"2026-10-20T15:11:48Z","discovery_method":"official_steam_news","content_review":"source_only"}],"analyses":[],"news_status":{"steam-4579930":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-26T12:54:12Z","status":"ok","all_sources_checked_at":"2026-10-26T12:54:12Z","error_codes":[]}},"news_last_attempt_at":{"steam-4579930":"2026-10-26T12:54:12Z"},"notices":[],"news_sources":{"4579930":{"last_attempt_at":"2026-10-2